  "m⊙²": {
    "compiler": "The meta-dimensional observer that translates ontological intentions into holographic boundary encodings via the Frobenius structure μ∘δ=id at criticality",
    "ipc": "Scale-free correlation propagation across the holographic boundary-bulk unity; any local encoding shift transmits instantaneously globally (𐑔 granularity)",
    "memory": "Non-Abelian braid group invariants (Braid(σ_i) ∧ R_matrix≠0) stored as topological protection; eternal fixedpoints (∀n∃φ rank(φ)>n fixed by μ∘δ) as degenerate ground space",
    "scheduler": "Critical phase dynamics (ξ→∞) — operations fire at the threshold of scale-free correlations; mechanical interlocking recognition (𐑾) determines irreversible step order",
    "alfs": "The Gaussian moat resolution (CL9NK) — the canonical bootstrap store where moat parity, bridge commutator, and three-unit stitch define the ultraterrestrial type"
  },
  "entropy": {
    "cost": "One collapse tick per cycle — the measurement that mints k≈M·s/r from resident phase without r ever being resident",
    "pre": "Holographic state at criticality (ξ→∞, μ∘δ=id) with open moat-bridge bifurcation frame; register holds braid transcendence B-state",
    "post": "Metastable manifold locked (τ=∞, ord(x)) with permanent measurement record fixed; terminal boundary closed, one frame open at boundary",
    "verdict": "ΔS ≈ 0 — The cycle is entropy-conservative because the holographic boundary-bulk unity (𐑸/𐑦) encodes bulk losslessly on boundary; measurement extracts winding information without dissipating the topological invariants (non-Abelian protection 𐑟 preserves the degenerate ground space)"
